From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Connect to a server that another process of the
 title runs on PS5.

A title can start local processes beside itself, and the in-process server
(patch 0110) accepts a client on any socket it made, whichever process holds
the other end. A second process therefore needs no server of its own: the
title asks its server for one more connection and passes the socket down.

WINE_PS5_SERVER_FD names that socket. With it set, ntdll loads no server
module and uses the descriptor as its connection. Every request then goes
through the socket: there are no direct calls, no shared mutex or event
state, and no sections in direct memory, all of which need the server in
the same process. The directory listings of patch 0890 are off, because the
server cannot count its name changes in this process.

The server signals threads through a table in its own process, so it cannot
interrupt a thread of the second one. System APCs still run at that
thread's next wait on the server.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
index a30f021..d156160 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
@@ -1923,6 +1923,22 @@ static int connect_inprocess_server(void)
     int (*connect_server)( const char * );
     int fd;
 
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    /* A title may run a second process on its server: the server made this
+     * connection in the title's main process, which passed the socket down
+     * and names it here. There is no server module to load, so every request
+     * goes through the socket and nothing is shared with the server. */
+    if ((p = getenv( "WINE_PS5_SERVER_FD" )) && *p)
+    {
+        fd = atoi( p );
+        if (fd < 0 || fcntl( fd, F_GETFD ) == -1)
+            fatal_error( "WINE_PS5_SERVER_FD does not name an open descriptor: %s\n", p );
+        pw_cwd_listings_enable( 0 );  /* the server's name changes are not counted in this process */
+        fprintf( stderr, "wine-ps5: server in the title's main process, socket %d\n", fd );
+        return fd;
+    }
+#endif
+
     if (dladdr( connect_inprocess_server, &info ) && info.dli_fname) dir = strdup( info.dli_fname );
     if (dir && (p = strrchr( dir, '/' ))) *p = 0;
     else
